 **Formulas:**
 The density is computed via fractal Brownian motion (fBm) accumulation [G]:
-$$\rho(x,y,z) = \sum_{i=0}^{4} A_i \cdot \mathcal{P}(M \cdot f_i \cdot x, M \cdot f_i \cdot y, M \cdot f_i \cdot z)$$
-where $\mathcal{P}$ is the Perlin noise function, $A_i = 0.5^i$ is the amplitude decay, $f_i = 2^i$ is the frequency multiplier, and $M=32$ is the base scale [S1, unofficial]. Since $N=2$, the $z$-coordinate is typically ignored or used as a phase/time variable [G].
