 ## Operating characteristics
 - **Time Complexity:** Low frame rates (~20 FPS for a $1024^3$ volume) due to complex GPU computations [S1, unofficial]. The use of 5 octaves of Perlin noise adds computational overhead [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Trades computation time for memory efficiency. Normals are computed on-the-fly. The brick pool used 430 MB, giving room for $42^3$ bricks. The node pool was small (4 MB) corresponding to $64^3$ entries. Using $16^3$ bricks, $1024^3$ indices can be referenced [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** Allows for an increase of detail in cloud simulation, especially when combined with complex shading for multiple scattering. On-the-fly noise creation on the GPU is more efficient than CPU evaluation and transfer [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Low frame rates due to complex GPU computations.
